# BFF — Provider webhook (M26-S04, UC-114)
# POST /v1/public/billing/webhooks/asaas: public, called by Asaas through the ikaro-web same-origin
# gateway (it attaches the shared-secret header; a direct call to the BFF needs X-Web-Internal-Key
# below). The BFF checks the `asaas-access-token` header against ASAAS_WEBHOOK_TOKEN (timing-safe;
# unset or wrong answers 401 and calls no backend), then forwards the JSON body to the backend.
# Answers EXACTLY 200 with an empty body (Asaas counts 201/204 as failures); a backend failure is
# forwarded as non-2xx so Asaas retries. Not rate limited (a retry storm must never meet a 429).
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run migration:run
#   3. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev  (port 3001)
#   4. pnpm --filter @ikaro/bff run dev      (port 3002)
#   5. ASAAS_WEBHOOK_TOKEN set in apps/bff/.env.local (any value, 1+ characters)
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@webInternalKey = {{$dotenv WEB_INTERNAL_KEY}}
@asaasToken     = {{$dotenv ASAAS_WEBHOOK_TOKEN}}

### Right token: 200 (the event is for an unknown customer, so nothing changes)
POST {{bffUrl}}/v1/public/billing/webhooks/asaas
X-Web-Internal-Key: {{webInternalKey}}
asaas-access-token: {{asaasToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "evt_00000000000000000000000000000000&1",
  "event": "PAYMENT_RECEIVED",
  "dateCreated": "2026-11-19 12:00:00",
  "payment": { "id": "pay_unknown", "customer": "cus_unknown", "value": 49.0 }
}

### Wrong token: 401, nothing reaches the backend
POST {{bffUrl}}/v1/public/billing/webhooks/asaas
X-Web-Internal-Key: {{webInternalKey}}
asaas-access-token: not-the-token
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Missing token: 401
POST {{bffUrl}}/v1/public/billing/webhooks/asaas
X-Web-Internal-Key: {{webInternalKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}
